              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Theresa Gwaltney Hayes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are THE best no-bakes I have made yet. Love them--so does everyone else!",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-24T12:49:07.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ChristineM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These came out fine, but I had to let them sit overnight to set properly. Even then, they came out softer that the typical no-bake oatmeal cookie - not that that's a bad thing, it just wasn't what I was expecting. The mixture was pretty loose when I placed them on the waxed paper - as usual, I used my cookie scoop to get fairly round, same-sized cookies. Flavor is excellent - fudgie, chocolatey and super sweet. I would definitely make these again, but I think I'll try boiling the mixture a bit longer (4 to 5 minutes) to get a firmer, more fudge-like consistency.",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-03T05:34:43.493Z"
          },
